From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: input: apple,z2-multitouch: Add the iPad Air
 (J72)

The iPad Air (J72) has an N1 controller like the iPad 5, with its
analog and core supplies from the PMIC, a reference clock, an attention
line and the display-sync pin states, but no GPIO rails. Add its
compatible and constraints.

Also fix the conditional supplies: ana-supply was declared twice, and
the "else" that forbids ana-supply and attn-gpios hung off the J71t
block, which also forbade the N61's analog supply. Split it into one
condition per property.

[Orchard: from thisiscamk/ipad-air-j72-linux 2a257d6,
 code/current/kernel/0001-j72-installed-kernel-snapshot.patch
 (Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/apple,z2-multitouch.yaml).
 The J72 block no longer pins the panel size, firmware name and
 calibration length (driver and board data), and the iPad mini 4 (J96),
 added in Orchard since, is kept in both conditions.]
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../touchscreen/apple,z2-multitouch.yaml      | 59 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/apple,z2-multitouch.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/apple,z2-multitouch.yaml
index b9d5dce04..4a89d6bbe 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/apple,z2-multitouch.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/apple,z2-multitouch.yaml
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ properties:
       - apple,j493-touchbar
       - apple,j71b-touchscreen
       - apple,j71t-touchscreen
+      - apple,j72-touchscreen
       - apple,j81-touchscreen
       - apple,j96-touchscreen
       - apple,j172-touchscreen
@@ -47,7 +48,8 @@ properties:
   ana-supply:
     description:
       Analog supply for the touchscreen controller, where a PMIC switch
-      rather than a GPIO provides it
+      rather than a GPIO provides it. On N61 this is the Chestnut
+      high-voltage switch
 
   hv-supply:
     description: High-voltage analog supply for the touchscreen controller
@@ -68,9 +70,6 @@ properties:
   clocks:
     maxItems: 1
 
-  ana-supply:
-    description: N61 analog touchscreen supply from the Chestnut high-voltage switch
-
   apple,z2-prox-cal-blob:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint8-array
     maxItems: 128
@@ -204,9 +203,61 @@ allOf:
         - clocks
         - ana-supply
         - power-ldo-gpios
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          const: apple,j72-touchscreen
+    then:
+      properties:
+        pinctrl-names:
+          items:
+            - const: display-sync-active
+            - const: display-sync-inactive
+        power-ana-gpios: false
+        power-ldo-gpios: false
+        display-sync-gpios: false
+        display-sync1-gpios: false
+        hv-supply: false
+        spi-cpha: false
+        spi-cpol: false
+        apple,z2-bpw16-min-len: false
+        apple,z2-no-init-ack: false
+      required:
+        - clocks
+        - ana-supply
+        - core-supply
+        - attn-gpios
+        - pinctrl-0
+        - pinctrl-1
+        - pinctrl-names
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          enum:
+            - apple,j71t-touchscreen
+            - apple,j72-touchscreen
+            - apple,j81-touchscreen
+            - apple,j96-touchscreen
+            - apple,n61-touchscreen
+    then:
+      properties:
+        ana-supply: true
     else:
       properties:
         ana-supply: false
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          enum:
+            - apple,j71t-touchscreen
+            - apple,j72-touchscreen
+            - apple,j81-touchscreen
+            - apple,j96-touchscreen
+    then:
+      properties:
+        attn-gpios: true
+    else:
+      properties:
         attn-gpios: false
   - if:
       properties:
